WEBVTT

00:09:29.726 --> 00:09:31.281
(Laughter)

00:09:31.305 --> 00:09:35.337
But what we also do is connect them
to individual cells within the antennae,

00:09:35.361 --> 00:09:36.512
which is incredible.

00:09:36.536 --> 00:09:38.834
You don't want to sneeze
when you're doing this,

00:09:38.858 --> 00:09:40.324
that's for sure.

00:09:40.348 --> 00:09:41.991
But what this does is it allows us

00:09:42.015 --> 00:09:45.578
to measure the electrical response
of the smell receptors in the antennae,

00:09:45.602 --> 00:09:48.951
and so we can see
what a mosquito is smelling.

00:09:48.975 --> 00:09:51.118
So I'm going to show you
what this looks like.

00:09:51.142 --> 00:09:52.293
Here's an insect's cell,

00:09:52.317 --> 00:09:55.269
and it will respond in a second
when I press this button,

00:09:55.293 --> 00:09:58.027
and you'll see it sort of ticking over
with this response.

00:09:58.051 --> 00:09:59.852
An odor will be blown over the cell,

00:09:59.876 --> 00:10:02.415
and it will go a bit crazy,
sort of blow a raspberry,